@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Generate operational and audit reports — End-to-end interaction
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Sodexo Administrator" as Actor
participant "Sodexo Employee Webapp" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Administration API" as Edge
participant "Accommodation Reporting Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events



group 1. Generate scoped operational, failure, reconciliation, or audit data.
  Actor -> Surface: Generate scoped operational, failure, reconciliation, or audit data
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/platform/reports
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Generate scoped operational, failure, reconciliation, or audit data.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Reporting Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Export or schedule a masked report for authorised recipients.
  Actor -> Surface: Export or schedule a masked report for authorised recipients
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/platform/reports/{reportId}/deliveries
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Export or schedule a masked report for authorised recipients.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Reporting Service data
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
